WEBVTT

00:12.980 --> 00:14.820
Akagami-kun, you're awake.

00:14.820 --> 00:19.200
Yes. I feel as though I've died and been reborn.

00:19.200 --> 00:20.080
As in reincarnated?

00:20.080 --> 00:22.400
I feel refreshed.

00:22.400 --> 00:24.830
Nothing could scare me now.

00:24.830 --> 00:26.890
Well, don't push yourself.

00:26.890 --> 00:31.760
Kiki-san and I are going out, 
but Mia and Kagura are up.

00:31.760 --> 00:33.880
Wait, why do you look terrified?!

00:34.340 --> 00:36.090
Good morning, Akagami.

00:36.460 --> 00:40.100
Good morning, Mia-san. Where is everyone else?

00:40.410 --> 00:43.280
Tsukuyo-san and Kurage-san are still asleep.

00:43.280 --> 00:45.350
Kagura is in her room using her computer.

00:50.530 --> 00:51.670
Kagura.

00:55.360 --> 00:56.340
Kagura.

00:57.870 --> 01:01.620
Initiate Operation 
Lovey-Dovey Akagami x Kagura!

01:03.060 --> 01:04.600
Where did that come from?

01:04.600 --> 01:06.540
I'll allow up to kissing.

01:06.540 --> 01:08.880
I still don't know what you're talking about.

01:08.880 --> 01:11.040
Akagami's scared of you.

01:11.040 --> 01:12.250
Oh, my.

01:12.640 --> 01:16.990
As though he's been deeply 
traumatized by something.

01:16.990 --> 01:19.010
Crap. I overdid it.

01:19.310 --> 01:22.750
I can't allow my best friend and 
brother in arms to be on bad terms.

01:22.750 --> 01:26.810
I want the two of you to get along 
as well as Akagami and I do.

01:26.810 --> 01:29.120
Don't you think that's a bit much?

01:29.120 --> 01:32.120
First, let's establish your 
impressions of each other.

01:32.120 --> 01:35.280
Akagami, how do you feel 
when you look at Kagura?

01:35.280 --> 01:38.680
Well, she makes my groin tingle.

01:38.680 --> 01:40.780
That's blatant sexual harassment.

01:40.780 --> 01:42.780
That's a positive impression, Kagura.

01:42.780 --> 01:45.410
That was enough to get him sent to court.

01:45.760 --> 01:48.390
Kagura, what do you think of Akagami?

01:49.540 --> 01:52.990
Akagami-san is a wonderful person.

01:52.990 --> 01:53.920
That's right!

01:53.920 --> 01:58.600
Akagami is an especially wonderful person!

01:58.600 --> 02:00.890
Aw, shucks.

02:00.890 --> 02:05.430
He's earnest and loyal, 
which is why I must drive him out.

02:05.430 --> 02:09.230
This actually sounds pretty promising!

02:09.230 --> 02:12.190
In that case, let's skip to the final stage.

02:15.190 --> 02:17.370
I'm locking you two in the shed 
until tomorrow morning.

02:17.370 --> 02:19.070
But it's morning right now!

02:19.650 --> 02:22.560
This is what made Akagami 
and I open up to each other.

02:22.560 --> 02:24.330
I'm sure it'll work great for you two, too.

02:25.030 --> 02:28.270
I'll arrange for you to perform 
Twister penance tonight.

02:28.270 --> 02:29.460
Mia-san!

02:32.160 --> 02:33.710
She got us.

02:34.080 --> 02:37.350
I never thought my own strategy 
would be used against me.

02:39.000 --> 02:39.930
Indeed.

02:39.930 --> 02:41.520
Though it beats being made to do

02:41.520 --> 02:44.590
the Hundred Poems by One Hundred Poets 
nonsense I taught her.

02:44.590 --> 02:46.430
That was you, too?

02:46.890 --> 02:50.030
<i>Is she responsible for all of 
Mia-san's misconceptions?</i>

02:50.030 --> 02:51.690
Oh, I know.

02:54.940 --> 02:58.860
If I say you assaulted me in here,

02:58.860 --> 03:01.950
that would be an easy way 
to drive you out of the temple.

03:06.150 --> 03:10.580
Why don't you tell Mia-san about my plan?

03:11.070 --> 03:14.160
It would put me in a difficult position.

03:14.160 --> 03:16.050
I'd never do that.

03:16.520 --> 03:19.400
I don't want to fight you, Kagura-sama.

03:19.400 --> 03:20.060
"Sama"?

03:20.060 --> 03:22.550
Ideally, I'd like to be friends.

03:23.280 --> 03:27.060
I value my relationship with you.

03:30.160 --> 03:32.670
Why are you hitting on me?

03:32.670 --> 03:33.560
Huh?!

03:33.560 --> 03:35.320
That's not what I was trying to do!

03:35.320 --> 03:37.280
From all the way over there, no less.

03:37.280 --> 03:40.070
I'm sorry. My body reacted 
before I could stop it.

03:41.250 --> 03:45.080
If you'd just seduce Mia-san 
and take responsibility for her,

03:45.080 --> 03:46.660
there would be no problem.

03:48.330 --> 03:50.740
Oh? What's this?

03:51.590 --> 03:52.460
What is it?

03:52.460 --> 03:56.030
It's nothing at all.

03:56.030 --> 03:57.460
It's open!

03:57.460 --> 03:59.390
It's the principle of the lever.

03:59.390 --> 04:01.470
But you very obviously kicked it!

04:03.330 --> 04:05.720
<i>Why didn't I realize it sooner?</i>

04:05.720 --> 04:07.300
<b>Take by Force...</b>

04:05.720 --> 04:07.300
<b>Make This</b>

04:06.000 --> 04:08.760
<i>Taking him by force is certainly an option.</i>

04:07.300 --> 04:08.060
<b>Make This</b>

04:07.300 --> 04:08.680
<b>Take by Force...</b>

04:07.300 --> 04:12.560
<b>Do This</b>

04:08.760 --> 04:14.480
<i>I'll make Akagami-san fall for Mia-san 
and bring him back to the Christoph family.</i>

04:12.560 --> 04:14.480
<b>Do This</b>

04:14.480 --> 04:17.440
Akagami-san, let's be friends.

04:17.440 --> 04:18.550
Huh?!

05:49.570 --> 05:53.660
<b>Episode 10:
I Just Got a Little Turned On</b>

05:52.360 --> 05:54.750
Wait, Akagami.

05:54.750 --> 05:59.000
I know we kissed once, but I'm not...

06:02.790 --> 06:04.510
We can't do this!

06:07.940 --> 06:10.010
Please, Akagami.

06:11.400 --> 06:15.020
At least be gentle.

06:19.490 --> 06:21.020
No...

06:33.140 --> 06:36.290
Good morning, Tsukuyo-oneechan.

06:36.980 --> 06:39.790
Good morning, Kurage-san.

06:40.720 --> 06:42.950
Could you let go of me?

06:44.180 --> 06:45.300
Okay.

06:45.680 --> 06:48.540
I'll buy you a chocolate parfait 
if you don't tell anyone.

06:49.440 --> 06:50.550
Make it extra large.

06:51.110 --> 06:52.250
Okay.

06:57.180 --> 07:00.010
<i>I can't believe I dreamed about that.</i>

07:00.010 --> 07:02.560
<i>Am I that unfulfilled?</i>

07:02.560 --> 07:03.770
Tsukuyo-san.

07:06.550 --> 07:08.070
Good morning.

07:09.890 --> 07:10.990
Hey.

07:10.990 --> 07:13.320
Time to make breakfast.

07:13.320 --> 07:17.830
All right. Here we go.

07:13.970 --> 07:16.010
<i>He looks so carefree.</i>

07:16.010 --> 07:21.580
<i>I only dreamed about that because he kissed me.</i>

07:22.710 --> 07:26.990
<i>Well, it was an accident. It's in the past now.</i>

07:26.990 --> 07:28.410
Akagami!

07:29.490 --> 07:31.470
What's on the menu today?

07:31.470 --> 07:33.520
We're having fried fish this morning.

07:33.520 --> 07:34.910
Fried fish!

07:34.100 --> 07:36.350
<i>Huh? Come to think of it...</i>

07:34.910 --> 07:36.350
Wait a little longer, okay?

07:36.350 --> 07:37.390
Okay!

07:37.390 --> 07:41.260
<i>When did those two get so close?</i>

07:45.110 --> 07:47.160
It's interesting, isn't it?

07:47.610 --> 07:51.050
Kagura, how are you so invisible?

07:52.610 --> 07:56.370
I believe this is the reason.

07:56.760 --> 07:58.150
A camera?

08:02.390 --> 08:04.640
<i>Akagami, it's too much.</i>

08:04.640 --> 08:07.130
<i>Go slower.</i>

08:07.780 --> 08:08.630
What?!

08:11.890 --> 08:13.380
<i>We're just getting started, Mia-san.</i>

08:13.660 --> 08:16.890
This is known as Twister penance.

08:16.890 --> 08:21.450
Hey, whoa! Wh-Wh-Wh-Why are 
you showing me a dirty video?!

08:22.740 --> 08:25.400
Wait... was that Akagami and Mia?

08:25.400 --> 08:28.400
Yes. Would you like to see more?

08:29.380 --> 08:31.100
Don't show me that!

08:31.100 --> 08:32.900
Just look at that bright light.

08:33.410 --> 08:35.660
<i>Those two are an item?</i>

08:36.210 --> 08:40.420
<i>But Mia hated Akagami at first.</i>

08:42.240 --> 08:43.540
Whoops.

08:43.540 --> 08:47.170
I'm sorry, Akagami. I tripped.

08:47.640 --> 08:49.530
Are you all right, Mia-san?

08:50.170 --> 08:51.420
I'm fine.

08:53.190 --> 08:56.180
I just got a little turned on.

08:56.180 --> 08:58.120
<i>She's totally in love with him!</i>

08:58.120 --> 09:00.760
<i>Not only that, but she's turned on?!</i>

09:04.690 --> 09:06.640
Let's begin the interrogation.

09:06.640 --> 09:08.380
I'm Kagura, the secretary.

09:08.380 --> 09:09.690
What's going on here?!

09:10.090 --> 09:13.190
We didn't need to invite Akagami-san?

09:13.610 --> 09:16.540
No. I can't look him in the face right now.

09:16.540 --> 09:18.950
Wait, Kagura, are you interested, too?

09:20.500 --> 09:24.120
I'm just interested in recording 
everything Mia-san does.

09:24.120 --> 09:26.260
I see. That's fine, then.

09:26.830 --> 09:30.840
The truth is, I've heard discipline 
around the temple has gotten a little lax.

09:30.840 --> 09:34.990
Not only that, but you're suspected 
to be at the center of it.

09:34.990 --> 09:35.840
Wha...

09:35.840 --> 09:37.680
I won't let you talk like that!

09:37.680 --> 09:41.100
There isn't a single shameful thing about me!

09:41.490 --> 09:44.620
Then you'd be willing to answer 
any question, wouldn't you?

09:44.620 --> 09:46.010
Of course!

09:47.270 --> 09:49.350
I see. In that case...

09:49.990 --> 09:54.110
Mia, do you like Akagami?

10:02.900 --> 10:04.750
I-I don't...

10:04.750 --> 10:05.780
What?

10:07.620 --> 10:10.060
Why are you asking me about that?

10:10.060 --> 10:10.780
What?

10:10.780 --> 10:11.950
Oh?

10:11.950 --> 10:14.640
But you've gotten a lot closer recently.

10:14.640 --> 10:17.010
Oh, that's what you meant.

10:17.370 --> 10:20.970
We're training partners. 
It's only natural for us to get along.

10:20.970 --> 10:22.960
I suppose I like him in that regard.

10:22.960 --> 10:23.930
Oh, my.

10:23.930 --> 10:25.600
Partners?

10:25.600 --> 10:28.490
We clashed over some 
misunderstandings at first,

10:28.490 --> 10:30.730
and now we've simply reconciled.

10:30.730 --> 10:32.230
Oh, I see.

10:32.590 --> 10:34.960
<i>So it was just my imagination.</i>

10:34.960 --> 10:36.150
Besides...

10:36.690 --> 10:40.420
Don't you think Akagami is 
the world's most handsome man?

10:40.420 --> 10:41.200
Huh?

10:41.200 --> 10:45.680
I actually came to Japan 
for spiritual training.

10:45.680 --> 10:48.710
I decided to fight my own worldly desires.

10:48.710 --> 10:52.270
In that regard, Akagami is the ideal partner.

10:52.270 --> 10:54.960
I have an incredibly handsome man by my side.

10:54.960 --> 10:59.970
Every day my desires are stoked, 
and I'm constantly turned on.

10:59.970 --> 11:04.080
I felt we were destined to meet.

11:04.080 --> 11:07.970
I wish I could spend my entire life with him.

11:10.520 --> 11:12.240
Let's continue the interrogation.

11:12.240 --> 11:14.110
But why?!

11:14.110 --> 11:17.440
Kagura! Why are you tying me up, Kagura?!

11:17.440 --> 11:20.170
<i>Destined to meet? Spend their lives together?</i>

11:17.440 --> 11:21.610
You're going to rip my arms off!

11:20.170 --> 11:24.620
<i>She more than just likes him, then!</i>

11:25.070 --> 11:26.910
<i>Does Akagami know this?</i>

11:26.910 --> 11:28.960
<i>Did he take advantage of that?</i>

11:28.960 --> 11:30.660
<i>But... But...</i>

11:31.120 --> 11:35.350
<i>He did lots of stuff to me, too. And...</i>

11:36.600 --> 11:41.840
I think I wanted to make you happy.

11:43.840 --> 11:45.720
<i>He even said that.</i>

11:45.720 --> 11:46.850
Oh?

11:47.210 --> 11:50.110
Tsukuyo-san, your face is bright red.

11:50.110 --> 11:53.930
You're that upset?! It's not like that!

11:54.670 --> 11:56.510
I'm not upset or anything!

11:56.510 --> 12:00.110
My, my. Please forgive me.

12:00.110 --> 12:06.570
I was under the impression you were jealous.

12:08.330 --> 12:11.950
What?! I don't have any feelings for Akagami!

12:11.950 --> 12:13.220
You called?

12:14.290 --> 12:16.290
It looks like you're having fun in...

12:24.640 --> 12:26.360
Akagami...

12:26.360 --> 12:27.430
Mia-san...

12:27.430 --> 12:29.810
<i>What in the world are they doing for fun?!</i>

12:30.110 --> 12:32.680
Tsukuyo-san, what is this?

12:33.150 --> 12:34.080
Tsukuyo-san?

12:34.080 --> 12:38.160
She's bright red. I wonder why.

12:34.190 --> 12:37.940
She's
bright
red

12:35.940 --> 12:37.940
I
wonder
why

12:38.160 --> 12:40.570
Don't look at my face.

12:40.570 --> 12:43.450
You've been doing something that 
makes you want to hide your face?!

12:45.560 --> 12:48.620
Akagami-san, would you like to join us?

12:48.620 --> 12:50.140
Of course I—

12:50.140 --> 12:51.860
Akagami!

12:52.720 --> 12:56.460
<i>I'll ask him directly about that video.</i>

12:56.460 --> 12:58.750
Kagura, show him the evidence!

12:58.750 --> 13:00.320
Okay.

13:00.320 --> 13:02.960
Oh? Where did my camera go?

13:02.960 --> 13:06.380
Kagura-san, is this your camera?

13:06.380 --> 13:07.720
Kurage?!

13:08.040 --> 13:10.890
<i>This is bad. That video is too explicit for her.</i>

13:10.890 --> 13:12.720
Don't play that video!

13:12.720 --> 13:14.660
Play what?

13:14.660 --> 13:16.730
I said don't!

13:16.730 --> 13:18.760
Whatever you do, don't watch it!

13:18.760 --> 13:20.510
They're panting for some reason.

13:20.510 --> 13:24.090
Kurage, listen to your older sister for once!

13:24.990 --> 13:29.680
<i>I accidentally showed my pure 
little sister that filthy video.</i>

13:29.680 --> 13:32.240
This looks like a fun game.

13:32.760 --> 13:33.720
Huh?

13:33.720 --> 13:35.020
What are you watching?

13:35.020 --> 13:39.400
Oh, you recorded our time in the storage shed.

13:40.130 --> 13:42.970
Huh? What? Game?

13:42.970 --> 13:46.380
Yeah. Look, there's a mat on the ground.

13:46.380 --> 13:47.500
Huh?

13:48.010 --> 13:52.260
O-Oh, I see. I totally thought...

13:52.260 --> 13:53.700
You totally thought?

13:54.890 --> 13:56.180
You totally thought what?

13:57.390 --> 13:59.530
What did you think this video was of?

14:05.140 --> 14:08.100
I'll buy you a strawberry parfait.

14:08.100 --> 14:09.300
Why?

14:10.160 --> 14:14.040
<b>No one who walks stealthily
is up to any good.</b>

14:18.930 --> 14:20.920
<i>We're broke!</i>

14:22.100 --> 14:25.460
<i>The temple's been hemorrhaging 
money over the New Year.</i>

14:25.460 --> 14:28.970
<i>We collected hardly anything 
from the parishioners.</i>

14:29.320 --> 14:33.220
<i>At this rate, we won't be able to save 
anything for repairs on the principle figure.</i>

14:33.220 --> 14:36.240
<i>No, I mustn't get discouraged.</i>

14:36.240 --> 14:39.230
<i>I'll do what I can.</i>

14:39.610 --> 14:42.060
<i>I'll start by saving on food expenses 
as much as possible.</i>

14:47.240 --> 14:49.630
Eek!

14:50.660 --> 14:54.040
What's wrong, Akagami? I heard 
what sounded like a young lady's scream!

14:54.040 --> 14:56.830
The rice... The rice...

14:56.830 --> 14:58.750
The rice is gone!

14:59.620 --> 15:01.080
What?!

15:01.080 --> 15:04.890
If we're out of rice, 
then shouldn't we simply buy more?

15:05.570 --> 15:07.340
Well, yes...

15:07.630 --> 15:09.530
But we're broke.

15:09.530 --> 15:11.970
Ah, I see.

15:13.380 --> 15:15.320
Fret not, Akagami.

15:15.320 --> 15:17.970
Japan has a system known as annual tribute.

15:17.970 --> 15:21.320
This should allow us to acquire rice for free.

15:21.320 --> 15:23.980
Mia-san, we don't do that in modern day Japan.

15:23.980 --> 15:26.880
Akagami-kun, did something happen?

15:26.880 --> 15:28.670
I thought I heard a young lady scream.

15:28.670 --> 15:31.900
Yuzuki-san, we're out of rice.

15:31.900 --> 15:35.200
Our stockpile finally ran out, huh?

15:35.200 --> 15:38.870
Guess we'll have to go collect tribute.

15:39.370 --> 15:40.520
Huh?

15:40.520 --> 15:41.750
Huh?

15:42.160 --> 15:43.510
That's for real?

15:45.010 --> 15:49.760
Mikazuki Temple owns a little bit of land. 
So do other temples.

15:50.280 --> 15:54.810
The people using the land pay us 
an annual tribute in the form of rice.

15:54.810 --> 15:57.010
In other words, it's like rent.

15:57.010 --> 15:58.600
I guess so.

15:58.600 --> 16:01.770
Why do you collect tribute instead of money?

16:01.770 --> 16:05.740
Because the goal of a temple 
isn't to make a profit.

16:05.740 --> 16:08.020
We offer our services out of kindness.

16:08.410 --> 16:09.820
I see.

16:10.200 --> 16:14.240
Sounds like you've been slacking 
in your studies, Akagami.

16:14.240 --> 16:16.410
<i>I feel so defeated.</i>

16:16.750 --> 16:20.270
Was it all right for us to come with you?

16:20.270 --> 16:21.900
It's not rude of us to suddenly show up?

16:21.900 --> 16:23.610
Of course it's fine.

16:23.610 --> 16:26.420
Rice is heavy, so I appreciate the help.

16:26.420 --> 16:30.500
Besides, meeting our parishioners 
is a part of your training.

16:31.040 --> 16:32.420
Training?

16:32.420 --> 16:35.930
The fourth key to achieving enlightenment:

16:35.930 --> 16:39.430
value all your bonds and be grateful for them.

16:39.430 --> 16:42.560
All things are bound together by our bonds.

16:39.470 --> 16:46.400
<b>Bond</b>

16:41.220 --> 16:46.400
<b>Cause</b>

16:42.560 --> 16:44.860
Everything has meaning.

16:42.980 --> 16:46.400
<b>Connection</b>

16:46.360 --> 16:50.970
It's no mere coincidence that 
you came to Mikazuki Temple, Mia,

16:50.970 --> 16:53.150
or that you're working here, Akagami-kun.

16:53.150 --> 16:54.640
That's...

16:54.640 --> 16:55.910
That's true.

16:55.910 --> 17:00.910
Since bonds are so important, we should 
express our gratitude for them every day.

17:00.910 --> 17:03.150
The people we're going to see

17:03.150 --> 17:06.120
became parishioners of Mikazuki Temple 
through their own connections, too.

17:06.120 --> 17:10.380
Mikazuki Temple

17:06.120 --> 17:12.570
We should know the people 
our temple exists to serve.

17:13.540 --> 17:18.540
All right. Then let's go see these people 
and express our gratitude!

17:18.540 --> 17:19.890
Yeah!

17:20.010 --> 17:22.640
Ain't got no rice. Get outta here.

17:29.400 --> 17:30.520
<i>Leave.</i>

17:33.750 --> 17:34.910
Yuzuki-san?!

17:34.910 --> 17:36.780
L-Let's try the next place.

17:37.940 --> 17:40.780
Tribute in this day and age? Now that's funny.

17:41.480 --> 17:43.200
Sir, we'd like some rice.

17:43.200 --> 17:44.460
What?

17:44.460 --> 17:45.880
I said, we're here to collect tribute.

17:45.880 --> 17:47.040
What?

17:47.550 --> 17:50.400
Sure, I'll give you some 
if you'll clean my house.

17:50.400 --> 17:51.290
What?!

17:51.760 --> 17:54.750
Why are we cleaning? Is this fate, as well?

17:54.750 --> 17:56.300
Now, now.

17:56.900 --> 17:59.300
The closet collapsed!

18:01.300 --> 18:03.160
What are we doing?

18:03.160 --> 18:05.420
We never got any rice in the end.

18:05.420 --> 18:10.560
Well, normally, parishioners 
deliver their tribute.

18:10.560 --> 18:13.640
The places we visited today are 
behind on their offerings because

18:13.640 --> 18:14.820
they've got a lot going on.

18:14.820 --> 18:17.340
In other words, they're troubled people.

18:17.340 --> 18:20.320
Well, uh... yeah.

18:20.720 --> 18:25.400
Next house! Our next stop's 
the last one, okay? Chin up!

18:27.220 --> 18:29.040
Welcome, Yuzuki-chan.

18:29.040 --> 18:30.830
Thanks for making the trip.

18:30.830 --> 18:32.760
Thank you for having us.

18:32.760 --> 18:36.720
It's fine. Oh, I haven't seen those two before.

18:36.720 --> 18:38.240
Thanks for coming all this way.

18:38.240 --> 18:40.090
I accidentally broke my leg, you know?

18:40.400 --> 18:42.480
The rice is in the yard.

18:42.480 --> 18:44.140
Take as much as you'd like.

18:45.180 --> 18:46.600
She's a goddess!

18:46.600 --> 18:49.350
What? You think I'm that beautiful?

18:51.780 --> 18:53.740
You've got some cute kids.

18:53.740 --> 18:55.480
Mom.

18:56.110 --> 18:57.600
Do we have guests?

18:57.600 --> 18:59.860
Hey, it's Yuzuki-oneechan!

18:59.860 --> 19:01.280
Hello.

19:01.280 --> 19:02.920
Aw, how cute.

19:02.920 --> 19:04.370
Welcome!

19:04.370 --> 19:06.490
Let's play. What do you want to do?

19:06.490 --> 19:07.870
Hooray!

19:07.870 --> 19:10.620
Now, now. She's busy.

19:10.620 --> 19:11.880
In that case...

19:11.880 --> 19:13.660
Show us your boobs!

19:13.660 --> 19:14.630
No.

19:14.630 --> 19:17.150
They ask every time.

19:14.630 --> 19:21.630
Boobs, boobs, boobs!

19:17.150 --> 19:20.700
Sorry. They just really love boobs, you know?

19:21.630 --> 19:24.030
Why are they so desperate to see them?

19:24.030 --> 19:26.080
Who wouldn't want to see—

19:26.080 --> 19:27.140
Akagami-kun?!

19:28.040 --> 19:31.770
<i>Am I mentally on the same 
level as young children?</i>

19:33.020 --> 19:35.770
You disappoint me, children.

19:35.770 --> 19:38.840
You won't grow up into 
decent adults acting like that.

19:40.220 --> 19:44.910
Only by defeating their worldly desires 
do people grow up right.

19:44.910 --> 19:46.440
I see.

19:46.440 --> 19:48.400
Okay, miss.

19:48.400 --> 19:49.790
I'm glad you understand.

19:49.790 --> 19:51.000
In that case...

19:51.000 --> 19:53.180
Show us a decent adult's boobs!

19:53.180 --> 19:54.920
How did you reach that conclusion?!

19:55.400 --> 19:57.610
Show us!

19:56.280 --> 19:59.090
Boobs, boobs, boobs!

19:58.020 --> 20:00.440
Oh, my. What a disaster.

20:01.120 --> 20:04.520
You're Akagami-kun, right? 
Yuzuki-chan's told me about you.

20:04.520 --> 20:06.880
Oh, I hadn't introduced myself yet.

20:06.880 --> 20:09.930
My name is Akagami. Nice to meet you.

20:11.300 --> 20:14.270
Sorry about all the fuss.

20:14.270 --> 20:17.440
It's fine. Compared to the other 
parishioners, this is nothing.

20:17.440 --> 20:19.440
Did you run into some trouble?

20:19.440 --> 20:22.570
Honestly, I never want to see them again.

20:23.720 --> 20:25.200
I like you.

20:25.780 --> 20:28.430
They didn't used to be like that.

20:28.430 --> 20:29.200
What?

20:29.660 --> 20:36.460
When Yuzuki-chan's mom, Tsukina-san, 
was around, nobody failed to pay tribute.

20:36.760 --> 20:39.870
After all, she was terrifying.

20:39.870 --> 20:42.400
She hit me more than once.

20:42.400 --> 20:43.220
What?!

20:43.220 --> 20:46.470
But she also made us feel secure.

20:46.860 --> 20:51.470
Everyone's anxious now that Tsukina-san's gone.

20:51.950 --> 20:55.480
They're wondering what's going 
to happen to Mikazuki Temple.

20:55.950 --> 20:58.620
Why did she leave?

20:58.620 --> 21:01.630
I don't know the details, either.

21:01.630 --> 21:04.240
I heard she lives at the main temple now.

21:04.240 --> 21:06.490
Akagami!

21:09.370 --> 21:11.340
Akagami-kun!

21:11.340 --> 21:12.880
Great boobs.

21:12.880 --> 21:14.320
Lucky.

21:14.320 --> 21:16.730
Cut that out, you pervy brats!

21:17.630 --> 21:19.690
Sorry about today.

21:19.690 --> 21:21.380
I know this doesn't make up for it, but...

21:24.310 --> 21:26.060
This is a huge amount.

21:26.060 --> 21:27.890
Be careful. They're heavy.

21:30.580 --> 21:32.390
They certainly are heavy.

21:33.910 --> 21:35.390
<i>Straw bags?</i>

21:35.780 --> 21:39.460
<i>Ah... I knew I'd seen these before.</i>

21:41.320 --> 21:42.730
<i>I saw them back then.</i>

21:43.400 --> 21:46.190
Is something the matter, Akagami-kun?

21:46.190 --> 21:47.160
No.

21:47.610 --> 21:50.500
I just felt a sense of destiny.

21:53.000 --> 21:54.290
I see.

21:54.290 --> 21:55.850
<i>That's right.</i>

21:55.850 --> 21:59.980
<i>I should be grateful I met Yuzuki-san 
and do everything I can to support her.</i>

22:00.440 --> 22:01.210
Hup.

22:02.430 --> 22:04.300
Shall we go, then?

22:06.550 --> 22:09.040
You're so strong, Yuzuki-san.

22:09.040 --> 22:11.660
Does she really need my support?

23:45.020 --> 24:00.040
<b>Next Time

The Body Doesn't Lie</b>

23:45.730 --> 23:47.340
What was your first dream of the year about?

23:47.340 --> 23:49.680
Akagami-san was hanging loose.

23:49.680 --> 23:50.600
What was loose?

23:50.600 --> 23:53.310
So were you and Tsukuyo-oneechan.

23:53.310 --> 23:54.560
What exactly were we doing?!

23:54.560 --> 23:57.550
Hanging loose and spreading the love.

23:57.550 --> 23:59.420
Love, huh?
